<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species faithfully reproduces Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 70.2/100, audit 2026-10-16-thompson-audit) and the assessments." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py; output: thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png; organism: Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/3cf7f8c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; other sources: On Growth and Form, chapter XVII, On the theory of transformations, or the comparison of related forms <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, On growth and form, 1917 Cambridge edition, Internet Archive item ongrowthform1917thom (Biodiversity Heritage Library contribution) <https://archive.org/download/ongrowthform1917thom/ongrowthform1917thom_jp2.zip/ongrowthform1917thom_jp2%2Fongrowthform1917thom_0769.jp2>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-93093-5>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/evo.13755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0112732>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.fn457gr> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match> ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 7.02e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Code-to-model traceability: 78/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Each step is tied to its source: the quoted passage to the Moebius reading, Fig. 376's oblique pencils to the second family, Fig. 374 to the affine part, Bookstein 1989 to the TPS, Claverie Fig. 1 to the drawn polygon and bars; every printed number names what it is compared with. Because Thompson gave no equations the trace ends at prose and a drawing, and the judgement that Fig. 376 is oblique rather than isogonal is made by eye, not measured on the scan. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L15–L23: why coaxial circles = Moebius <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L15-L23>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L243–L247: coaxial(): Fig. 374 / Fig. 376 reading <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L243-L247>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L163–L166: gpa(): orientation convention tied to Thompson's figures <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L163-L166>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L398–L408: panel titles name the figure each grid corresponds to <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L398-L408>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Thompson published no equations, so fidelity is to his words and figure. \"Coaxial circles\" is formalised as the Moebius group, the only maps that carry straight lines to circles, and the script states that reading in the docstring; because Fig. 376's two pencils meet obliquely, a second family (affine then Moebius) is fitted so that the figure as drawn is covered and not only its stated idealisation. The alternative Thompson compares against (\"rectilinear co-ordinates\", i.e. the identity/similarity) and the one he does not (affine) are fitted the same way, and the exact deformation is the thin-plate spline of Bookstein 1989, the standard successor to the method. The fitters are checked on synthetic maps before the real fit. Not higher because Thompson's own drawn grid is not digitised and compared with the fitted one (the comparison is grid-family to data, not his constants to the fitted constants); because his \"typical Scaroid fish\" and unnamed Pomacanthus are replaced by genus Procrustes means, which is the right test of the general claim but not of his drawing; and because the fish are 17 landmarks, not the outline Thompson deformed, so curvature between landmarks is untested. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L5–L23: the claim quoted; the reading of coaxial circles as a Moebius map <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L5-L23>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L47–L66: what is computed: the five families, noise floor, context, LOO <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L47-L66>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L210–L269: moebius()/fit_moebius()/coaxial()/fit_coaxial(): the two coaxial families, started from the affine fit, several c starts <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L210-L269>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L272–L290: tps_fit()/tps_apply(): Bookstein 1989 with bending energy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L272-L290>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L305–L313: self_test(): known maps recovered <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L305-L313>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Morphometric validation: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The whole script is morphometric validation on real specimens: Procrustes distance, residual of each family, explained share, the within-genus RMS as a noise floor with its species range, a leave-one-landmark-out prediction that shows the family has no predictive value for held-out landmarks, the depth/length change and the affine singular-value ratio that explain why a conformal map cannot work, the per-landmark residual ranking, the position of the pair among all 3782 genus pairs and the Scarus -> Chaetodon distribution. The measurements are reproduced independently in the audit sidecar. Not higher because there is no published value to compare against beyond the species count (791 against \"nearly 800\"; Thompson's claim has no numbers and nobody has fitted this pair before, so the only external anchor is the data set itself); digitising error is not estimated (one specimen per species, no replicate), so the noise floor mixes species and measurement variance; and the genus means rest on 9 Pomacanthus species. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L293–L302: all_fits(): residuals and explained shares <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L293-L302>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L316–L320: within_group_rms(): the noise floor <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L316-L320>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L534–L560: main(): per-landmark residuals, depth/length, LOO, context percentile, Chaetodon, verdict <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L534-L560>; morphoeval/measure_outputs.py L471–L526: measure_thompson_fish(): the same quantities in the sidecar <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/morphoeval/measure_outputs.py#L471-L526>; thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png (generated output, not in repo): panels C and D — thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 3cf7f8c, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): species in the landmark table = 791 count (reference 791, Friedman et al. 2019, Dryad 10.5061/dryad.fn457gr (Claverie & Wainwright 2014 landmarks), CC0: 'nearly 800 species') [rows of trimmed_tps_Claverie2014.csv (sha256 checked)]; Scarus species = 22 count [rows whose genus is Scarus]; Pomacanthus species = 9 count [rows whose genus is Pomacanthus]; Procrustes distance, Scarus mean to Pomacanthus mean = 0.0312 Procrustes units (RMS per landmark) [RMS landmark distance after optimal similarity superimposition of the genus means (unit centroid size)]; affine residual = 0.0259 Procrustes units [RMS after a least-squares affine map (6 parameters)] — explains 30.9 % of the Procrustes distance; Moebius residual (isogonal coaxial circles) = 0.0311 Procrustes units [RMS after a least-squares Moebius map z -> (az+b)/(cz+1), the conformal map that turns the Cartesian grid into two orthogonal pencils of coaxial circles] — explains 0.8 %: a conformal map cannot change the depth/length ratio; oblique coaxial-circle residual = 0.0256 Procrustes units [RMS after an affine map followed by z -> z/(cz+1) (8 parameters): coaxial circles whose two pencils need not be orthogonal, the family Thompson's Fig. 376 belongs to as drawn] — explains 32.4 %; thin-plate spline bending energy = 0.6778 dimensionless [bending energy of the exact TPS from the Scarus mean to the Pomacanthus mean (Bookstein 1989)]; within-Pomacanthus RMS (noise floor) = 0.0132 Procrustes units [RMS of the Pomacanthus species about their own Procrustes mean] — species range 0.0090-0.0180; within-Scarus 0.0099; leave-one-landmark-out RMS of the oblique coaxial family = 0.0371 Procrustes units [each landmark predicted by the 8-parameter map fitted to the other 16] — compare with the Procrustes distance: the family has no predictive value for held-out landmarks if it is not smaller; depth/length, Scarus mean = 0.3772 ratio [landmark extent in y over extent in x]; depth/length, Pomacanthus mean = 0.5873 ratio [landmark extent in y over extent in x]; percentile of Scarus -> Pomacanthus among all genus pairs (oblique coaxial, explained share) = 31.1475 percent [share of the 3782 ordered pairs of genus means (genera with >= 3 spp.) explained less well] — median pair 43 %; Scarus -> Chaetodon spp., median explained by oblique coaxial circles = 35.12 percent [median over the 54 Chaetodon species] — range 12-61 %." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — MorphoEval overall 70.2/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Loads and hash-checks the 791-species x 17-landmark table; generalised Procrustes superimposition (unit centroid size, no reflection), rotated so the snout-to-peduncle axis is horizontal; genus means. From the Scarus mean to the Pomacanthus mean fits five maps - similarity (Procrustes distance 0.0312), affine (residual 0.0259, 31 % of the squared distance explained), Moebius z -> (az+b)/(cz+1) (0.0311, 0.8 %; Thompson's \"system of coaxial circles\" read as isogonal), affine then Moebius (0.0256, 32 %; oblique coaxial circles as Fig. 376 is drawn) and the thin-plate spline (exact, bending energy 0.678) - after checking that the two non-linear fitters recover known maps to 1e-17. Reports the within-Pomacanthus RMS (0.0132, species 0.0090-0.0180) and within-Scarus RMS (0.0099) as the noise floor, a leave-one-landmark-out RMS for the oblique family (0.0371, above the 0.0312 of no deformation), the depth/length change (0.377 -> 0.587; affine singular-value ratio 1.27), the per-landmark residuals after the affine fit (largest LM7, LM2, LM4, LM8), the same fits for all 3782 ordered pairs of 62 genus means (median explained by oblique coaxial circles 43 %; this pair at the 31st percentile) and Scarus -> each Chaetodon species (12-61 %, median 35 %). Figure: Thompson's Figs. 375-376 cropped from the hash-pinned scan beside the superimposed real species with numbered landmarks; five grid panels carrying the Scarus mean and its grid under each map with residual vectors to the real Pomacanthus mean; the residual ladder against the noise floors; the context scatter. GIF: the best grid of Thompson's family and the thin-plate spline grid morphing side by side. Overall 70.2/100 (faithfulness 65.6, reproducibility 80.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 3cf7f8c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 55, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 75. Output judged: thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 3cf7f8c, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add outlines (semilandmarks along the body profile, or the Bishop Museum photographs of one Scarus and one Pomacanthus) so the comparison is of the form Thompson deformed, not 17 points.",
        "remediation needed: Digitise Thompson's drawn grid of Fig. 376 from the pinned scan, fit the Moebius constants to it, and compare them with the constants fitted to the species, so his drawing is tested and not only his family.",
        "remediation needed: Estimate digitising error (replicate landmarking of a few photographs) so the noise floor can be separated into species and measurement variance.",
        "remediation needed: Pin the Python 3.14 environment (exact versions) in requirements or a lock file.",
        "remediation needed: Sweep the complex constant c at fixed affine part in a panel, and report the fitted constants for the 54 Chaetodon species to test \"small variations in the values of the constants\" directly." ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.02e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Parameter expressivity: 55/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Thompson's claim has constants (\"small variations in the values of the constants of the coaxial curves\" for the other Chaetodonts) and the script treats them as such: the GIF moves the eight constants of the oblique family along a straight path from the identity to the fitted values and shows the grid bending into coaxial circles while the fish deepens, which is the monotone visible effect the dimension asks for. The Chaetodont claim is tested by fitting the family to each of the 54 Chaetodon species. Not higher because the constants are not swept one at a time (no panel shows what the complex c alone does to the grid at fixed affine part), the fitted constants for the Chaetodon species are not reported or plotted, so \"small variations\" is tested only through the explained share, and the family's two free-form parameters (the affine part) are not Thompson's. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L465–L499: animate(): straight path in parameter space from identity to the fitted map <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L465-L499>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L243–L253: coaxial(): the eight constants and their roles <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L243-L253>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L517–L520: Scarus -> each Chaetodon species <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L517-L520>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Reproducibility package: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic (Levenberg-Marquardt from fixed starts, seeded self-test), invocation and outputs documented, the data file is in the repository and hash-checked, the only network fetch is optional (--no-scan) and hash-checked, re-runs give identical numbers. Dependencies are in requirements.txt with lower bounds only and the known-good environment is recorded only in this audit; the GIF takes ~2 min because each frame refits a thin-plate spline and re-renders. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L67–L73: documented invocation and outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L67-L73>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L523–L580: main(): flags, offline fallback for the scan <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L523-L580>; requirements.txt L1–L7: lower bounds only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/requirements.txt#L1-L7>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Thompson is cited to page and figure with the public-domain scan pinned to one JPEG-2000 leaf by SHA-256; the landmark table is cited to its Dryad DOI, licence and byte size and vendored with its SHA-256 checked on every run (and kept byte-identical through git by a -text attribute); the landmark definitions are cited to Claverie & Wainwright 2014 Fig. 1 and the paper that released the file to its DOI; Bookstein 1978 and 1989 are cited for the method's history and the TPS. Short of full marks because the landmark semantics were read off a figure (the paper has no landmark table) and because the Dryad download could not be scripted (browser challenge), so the vendored file's provenance rests on the recorded hash rather than on a reproducible fetch. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L25–L45: data and scan provenance in the docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L25-L45>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L87–L97: DATA_SHA256, DATA_DRYAD, SCAN_URL, SCAN_SHA256 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L87-L97>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L116–L141: load_landmarks()/fetch_scan(): both hashes enforced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L116-L141>; datasets/thompson/README.md L1–L30: sources table, licences, why vendored, landmark definitions <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/datasets/thompson/README.md#L1-L30>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Morphological realism / specimen match: 55/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The specimens are the 791 real species, and Thompson's own figure is placed beside them from the hash-pinned scan, so the side-by-side the dimension asks for is there. Judged on it, the fish Thompson's family carries does not match the real Pomacanthus at species resolution: the best coaxial grid leaves a residual twice the spread of the nine Pomacanthus species about their mean, the residual vectors in panel B'' show where (anal fin, upper jaw, dorsal-fin end), and the thin-plate grid in panel B'''' shows the deformation the data demand is not a system of circles. Distinct morphologies are distinct (Scarus and Pomacanthus means differ by 0.031, three times the within-genus spread). Scored in the middle because the comparison is honest and legible but the rendering is a 17-landmark polygon with four bars, not an outline or a photograph: the body profile, the fin shapes and the head that make a Pomacanthus recognisable are not shown, and Thompson's drawn grid is displayed, not overlaid on the fitted one. Evidence: thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png (generated output, not in repo): panels A (Thompson), A'/A'' (real species), B-B'''' (grids with residuals), C, D — thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 3cf7f8c, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L356–L362: scan_crop(): Figs. 375-376 from the pinned page <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L356-L362>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L392–L420: row B: each family's grid and fish with residual vectors to the real mean <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L392-L420>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L102–L104: OUTLINE/WIRES: what of the fish is drawn <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L102-L104>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus> rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species faithfully reproduces Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view morphology" ;
    dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species (thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Code-to-model traceability' for Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view" ;
    dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" .

